course: dictionary
lesson: 9194
title: Sodium
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sodium is a chemical element, one of the basic substances that everything is made from. Its symbol is Na. «Sodium is a soft metal that fizzes wildly in water» tells you what it is like: soft, silvery-white, and very reactive.
explain: Sodium is never found pure in nature, because it reacts so easily with other things. Instead it is joined to other elements. «Salt is made of sodium and chlorine» shows this: sodium joins with chlorine to make a safe new substance.
explain: You will often meet sodium on food labels. Sodium on a label usually means salt, so checking it helps you know how much salt you are eating.
fact: Sodium is a soft, silvery-white metal with the symbol Na.
fact: Sodium reacts strongly with water, sometimes fizzing and catching fire.
fact: Sodium is never found pure in nature.
fact: «Sodium chloride» is the chemical name for common table salt.
fact: «Sodium» on a food label usually means salt in the food.
exercise: What is the symbol for sodium? | So | *Na | Sd | Od
exercise: «Sodium is a soft metal that fizzes wildly in water.» What does this tell you sodium does with water? | It turns it into sugar | It soaks it up like a sponge | It has no effect at all | *It reacts strongly with it
exercise: Ella reads a food label that says «sodium» and asks what it means. What does it usually mean? | *Salt in the food | A metal you can't eat | Sugar in the food | Fat in the food
test: Which two elements are joined to make salt? | Iron and gold | Sodium and oxygen | Carbon and hydrogen | *Sodium and chlorine
test: Why is sodium never found pure in nature? | It only forms when the weather is hot | It is too heavy to stay on the ground | It is hidden under the sea | *It reacts so strongly with other things
exam: Which phrase is the name of baking soda? | Sodium vapour | Low sodium | *Sodium bicarbonate | Sodium chloride
